  "body": "## Problem\n\nFound by a review of PR #3872 (#3748) on `main` `1fe369fab`, after the merge. A plain 2D Pocket with Outside containment and no stock known (the #3567 band case):\n\n- **With Arc:** the automatic dead-end ramp is still there. There are 8 \"ramp along the pass instead\" entries from `descent_dive::entry_restart`, over 1411 mm². This is the same as before the PR. The maintainer's rule on #3748: remove each automatic entry that the user did not select.\n- **With Plunge:** the tool plunges 9 times into uncut stock, with no note and no warning. The advice depends on `AirRoom`, and that case has no air room.\n- The stand-in notes (`descent_dive.rs:272` and `:284`, `air_entry.rs:241-247`) are notes only. `entry_status_lines` drops them, and no Warning is posted. So the user sees nothing.\n- Pins 2 and 3 of #3748 are green on `main` with this behaviour, so they do not pin it.\n\n## Why P1\n\nA plunge into uncut stock with no warning is an unsafe result that passes silently (Prime Directive). The maintainer ordered that each outcome issue of the #3741 family is P1.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Remove the automatic dead-end ramp for a selected Arc on a plain Outside pocket. If no air entry is possible, refuse the entry with a named diagnostic, or use a safe entry and name it in a **Warning**, not a note.\n- A selected Plunge into uncut stock gives exactly one Warning that names the plunge, on the operation and in the status line.\n- `entry_status_lines` shows each stand-in entry.\n- Pins, red on `main` `1fe369fab` first: a plain Outside pocket with no stock (1) with Arc has no automatic ramp, or names it as a Warning; (2) with Plunge has a Warning for each plunge into stock.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Related: #3748 (closed by #3872), #3567, #3746, #3843.\n- Review comment: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/3872#issuecomment-7130985919\n",
